"Two things I did not do
Three sibling paths have the identical hole and I've left them for you to decide: removeMappingOutput (deleting one output strands that output's DeckLink — closest to this bug), handleRemoveEdge (pulling just a cable), and handleRemoveAllEdges (releases nothing at all). I held off on edge removal specifically because you may pull and re-plug a cable routinely, and releasing on every unplug is a behaviour change that should be a decision, not something inherited from this fix.

A trap worth flagging: src/config/build-caspar-config-decklink.js and build-caspar-config-routing.js have no requires anywhere in src/. They're dead twins of the real generator pipeline, carrying their own stale copies of assignDecklinkToScreen. I nearly read the wrong one. Worth deleting under a hygiene pass.

Suite is 2010 tests, 2008 pass, 0 fail. Client built and kiosk reloaded, so the new endpoint is live.

Both of today's DeckLink fixes still need a Caspar restart to take effect in the generated config, and neither live delete has been exercised — that's the QA I owe you."
